+    # Optional cross-encoder reranking.
+    #
+    # CE-1: this block used to blend the cross-encoder score into only the top
+    # `k * 2` candidates while every other candidate kept its raw RRF score, and
+    # then sorted both kinds together in one list. ms-marco cross-encoders emit
+    # raw logits that are routinely negative (measured range on this host:
+    # -11.4 .. +3.3), so a blended candidate scored ~0.5*rrf + 0.5*ce and could
+    # fall BELOW an unblended candidate still sitting at its raw rrf (~0.007).
+    # The reranker could therefore push the best candidates out of the returned
+    # window while `_retrieval.cross_encoder` still reported True.
+    #
+    # The fix has three parts:
+    #   1. score every candidate, so no two candidates compete on different
+    #      scales;
+    #   2. squash the logits to (0, 1) before blending, so the two terms are
+    #      commensurate and the blend cannot invert the ordering;
+    #   3. apply the rerank atomically - on any failure, revert to the RRF
+    #      ordering and say so, rather than returning a half-mutated list.
+    rerank_applied = False
+    rerank_error = None
     if USE_CROSS_ENCODER and sorted_results:
